  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">EU Support to End Sexual and Gender-based Violence (SGBV) in Nigeria</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall objective of the proposed intervention is to support Nigeria&#xbf;s effort to reduce sexual and gender-based violence (SGBV) at federal, state and local levels. Building on the positive outcomes of the EU-UN Spotlight Initiative which came to an end in 2023, the ongoing Rule of Law and Anti-Corruption Programme II (RoLAC II) and considering the unprecedented political commitment to `break the silence on SGBV&#xbf;, this action will focus on the amendment and implementation of key legal and policy frameworks and the enactment of complementary laws; the expanded provision of essential services for survivors through the Sexual Assault Referral Centres &#xbf; SARCs, shelters, legal aid, and specialised Courts and Tribunal; and innovative advocacy to prevent and change harmful social norms especially through media, education/culture, faith and traditional entities. It will also strengthen capacities of stakeholders (public institutions, CSOs, communities and individuals/rights-holders).</narrative>
  </description>
